.\" Man page for elle(1)
.\" Generated for ELLE 0.1.0
.TH ELLE 1 "January 2025" "ELLE 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
elle \- natural language interface for system administration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B elle
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B elle
is a local-first, agentic system layer for Ubuntu that converts
kernel-level telemetry into natural language insight and safe system
operations. It provides both an interactive REPL and one-shot command
execution.
.PP
All inputs are classified into intents before execution. System-mutating
actions require explicit confirmation. Privileged operations are gated
through Polkit authentication.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Use specified configuration file instead of defaults.
.SH COMMANDS
When run without arguments, elle enters interactive REPL mode. Commands
can also be passed as arguments for one-shot execution.
.SS Prefix Commands
.TP
.B /ask \fIQUESTION\fR
Force classification as a system question (explanation/diagnosis).
.TP
.B /do \fITASK\fR
Force classification as a system task (requested change).
.TP
.B /sh \fICOMMAND\fR
Force shell passthrough (safe commands only).
.TP
.B /fix
Diagnose and repair the last failed command.
.SS Navigation Commands
.TP
.B status
Display current system status overview.
.TP
.B events
Show recent telemetry events from elled.
.TP
.B logs \fR[\fIFILTER\fR]
Display filtered system logs.
.SS Reactive Function Commands
.TP
.B /react create
Create a new reactive function from natural language.
.TP
.B /react list
List all reactive functions.
.TP
.B /react show \fIID\fR
Show details of a reactive function.
.TP
.B /react enable \fIID\fR
Enable a reactive function.
.TP
.B /react disable \fIID\fR
Disable a reactive function.
.TP
.B /react delete \fIID\fR
Delete a reactive function.
.TP
.B /react history \fR[\fIID\fR]
Show execution history.
.TP
.B /react test \fIID\fR
Test a reactive function with mock event.
.SS GUI Automation Commands
.TP
.B /learn \fIAPPLICATION\fR
Learn the UI structure of an application.
.TP
.B /learn list
List learned applications.
.TP
.B /learn show \fIAPPLICATION\fR
Show recipe for an application.
.TP
.B /learn rebuild \fIAPPLICATION\fR
Rebuild recipe for an application.
.TP
.B /learn delete \fIAPPLICATION\fR
Delete recipe for an application.
.SS Meta Commands
.TP
.B help
Display help information.
.TP
.B exit
Exit the REPL.
.TP
.B config
Display current configuration.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Check disk usage:
$ elle "how much disk space is left?"
.TP
Execute a system task:
$ elle "/do enable ufw with default deny incoming"
.TP
Run a shell command:
$ elle "/sh df -h"
.TP
Fix a failed command:
$ elle "/fix"
.TP
Interactive mode:
$ elle
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/elle/elle.toml
System-wide configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/elle/elle.toml
User configuration file (overrides system config).
.TP
.I /var/lib/elle/
State directory containing databases:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
elle.db \- Event database
.IP \(bu 2
manvault.db \- Man page index
.IP \(bu 2
incidents.db \- Incident vault
.IP \(bu 2
reactive.db \- Reactive functions
.IP \(bu 2
recipes.db \- GUI automation recipes
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ELLE_LOG_LEVEL
Log verbosity level (DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR). Default: INFO.
.TP
.B OLLAMA_HOST
Ollama server address. Default: http://localhost:11434.
.SH SECURITY
.B elle
enforces a strict denylist preventing execution of dangerous commands
including: rm -rf /, mkfs, dd to disk devices, fork bombs, recursive
chmod 777, curl|bash, sudo, and system shutdown commands.
.PP
System-mutating operations follow an Explain-Plan-Confirm-Apply workflow.
Privileged actions require Polkit authentication.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion.
.TP
.B 1
General error.
.TP
.B 2
Command blocked by denylist.
